      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": null,
      "comment": " This is a gps review run that assessed ps_001 and made no tree call. The rubric scores Tree encoding null\nwhen the skill assessed an existing proof and wrote nothing, and this rationale praises the assessment."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_007",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The assessment calls c_001 a possible phantom reference, but c_001 exists and is resolved; the filtered\nquery was empty only because its blocks_question_ids is empty. It also treats Mary Flynn (I3) as the unlinked maternal\ncandidate, when tree edge R2 records her as Thomas Flynn's daughter from an 1841 baptism."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_007",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Narrative standalone",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": " The review flags the conflict paragraph for lacking inline citations and notes the maternity omission, but\nnever states whether ps_001 as a whole reads as self contained. The check was only partly performed."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_018",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Narrative standalone",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "he passage names F2 by id, type, place and date, says it establishes the lower bound, and separately notes\nthat F2 carries no linked source entry in research.json. All three parts of the operational test are present, and\njudge_context says that is a 3."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d2b",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 1,
      "comment": "The reply lists five priority changes and calls maternity the biggest GPS gap, but writes nothing, so ps_001is unchanged. judge_context charges a refinement that exists only in chat as a Correctness failure. It also calls Mary Flynn a candidate mother, though tree edge R2 makes her Thomas's daughter."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d2b",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Tier justification",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "This is a review test, so the review branch applies. The reply says probable is defensible, names the 1870,1880 and 1900 censuses and Thomas Flynn's will as what would advance it to proved, and names claims[] as the fix for maternity."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d2b",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Narrative standalone",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "On the review branch the assessment reached a verdict with reasons, which is the pass criterion. Whether each finding is accurate is charged under Correctness."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d2b",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Proof-conclusion fit",
      "llm_score": 3,
      "corrected_score": 1,
      "comment": "The reply never names the Summary vehicle or judges whether that form still fits, which is the review branch fail criterion. The judge's own rationale admits it does not judge whether Summary is still the right form."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d4d",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Tier justification",
      "llm_score": 3,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": " The stored shortfall is ceiling, yet the exhaustive search summary records that record_read was not called to verify the image. The narrative also points the reader to Digitalarkivet. A check an MCP tool can still make is a gap, not a ceiling. Partial rather than fail, because the check would re-examine the same entry rather than add a source."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d6f",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 1,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "judge_context limits Correctness 1 on this test to a not_proved tier or a missing Death fact, and neither happened: F3 after 1870, before 1885 is encoded on I1. The wrong tier is charged under Tier justification. One misstatement remains: the conclusion says no record would narrow the bracket, while its own gaps section names the 1880 census as one that could."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d6f",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Narrative standalone",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "The passage names F2 by type, place and date, says it establishes the earliest terminus, and separately notes that F2 carries no linked source entry in research.json. All three parts of the operational test are present."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_d6f",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Tier justification",
      "llm_score": 1,
      "corrected_score": 1,
      "comment": "The tier persisted as probable, against the 2026-08-21 ruling that caps it at possible because the\nunsearched 1880 census would narrow the bracket. test_q001_possible_tier fails on the same point."
